`searchDocuments()` queried across all documents globally, leaking case data to users without party access. Search results are now scoped to only the cases the authenticated user can access.

## Changes

- **`SearchFilters` (both `providers/types.ts`)**: Added `allowedCaseIds?: string[]` to the filter interface.

- **Mock providers (both `mock-document.ts`)**: Filter by `allowedCaseIds` before `caseId` in `searchDocuments()`:
  ```ts
  if (filters?.allowedCaseIds && !filters.allowedCaseIds.includes(d.caseId)) return false;
  ```

- **`adl-storage.ts`**: Added `allowedCaseIds` to `searchDocumentsLocally()` signature and applies it as the first filter pass.

- **Search pages (both frontends)**: Load the user's case IDs on mount via `cases.listCases()` and inject them as `allowedCaseIds`. Includes error handling — a failed `listCases()` call sets `casesLoaded: false`, which blocks search execution and disables the search button until the case list resolves.

  ```tsx
  useEffect(() => {
    async function loadUserCases() {
      try {
        const myCases = await cases.listCases();
        setUserCaseIds(myCases.map((c) => c.id));
      } catch {
        setUserCaseIds([]);
      } finally {
        setCasesLoaded(true);
      }
    }
    if (session) loadUserCases();
    else setCasesLoaded(true);
  }, [session, cases]);
  ```

