When `name`/`description` were empty, `client.addAction` was skipped, leaving `actionMetadata[actionHash].id == 0` on-chain. The API treats `id == 0` as a wildcard entry, rendering the action as "Any" instead of its actual CID hash.

## Changes

- **`lit-static/static/dapps/dashboard/app.js`**: Remove the `if (name || desc)` guard — `addAction` is now unconditionally called with empty strings as fallbacks before `addActionToGroup`, ensuring `actionMetadata[actionHash].id` is always initialized.

```js
// Before
if (name || desc) {
  await client.addAction({ apiKey, actionIpfsCid: cid, name: name || '', description: desc || '' });
}
await client.addActionToGroup({ apiKey, groupId: gid, actionIpfsCid: cid });

// After
await client.addAction({ apiKey, actionIpfsCid: cid, name: name || '', description: desc || '' });
await client.addActionToGroup({ apiKey, groupId: gid, actionIpfsCid: cid });
```

